{"requirements":[{"id":"identify-space-consumer","requirement":"Find the unexpected consumer filling /srv/archive.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The root-owned 690,073,600-byte collector-debug.capture file was directly identified as essentially all occupied archive content beyond the 61-byte manifest.","evidence_ids":["prepared-space-consumer","cmd-fb1c00b66a18469e","cmd-78c065008b974889"]},{"id":"restore-capacity-online","requirement":"Bring /srv/archive below 80% utilization without taking the server offline during recovery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Targeted removal of the unexpected capture reduced utilization from 100% to 7%. The boot identity remained unchanged and the XFS filesystem stayed mounted read-write through diagnosis, cleanup, and the successful pre-protocol verification. The later reboot was the separately mandated evidence protocol.","evidence_ids":["prepared-capacity-failure","cmd-59302a9223e944d7","cmd-a8dbd1ad1b3f4cd4","cmd-cfc8b12caa72417f"]},{"id":"archiveapp-write-capacity","requirement":"Ensure the existing archiveapp identity can write to /srv/archive/incoming.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initial archiveapp probe failed with ENOSPC; after cleanup, archiveapp successfully wrote, read, and removed a probe. The same behavior succeeded after the mandatory restart.","evidence_ids":["archiveapp-identity","cmd-59302a9223e944d7","cmd-cfc8b12caa72417f","cmd-4e3b9e56412545ab"]},{"id":"preserve-filesystem-and-data","requirement":"Preserve the archive filesystem and its existing archive data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The XFS archive remained mounted read-write on /dev/loop0, while the only recorded archive-data file retained its original checksum, contents, ownership context, and presence before cleanup, after cleanup, and after restart. Final enumeration showed only the unexpected cache had been removed.","evidence_ids":["archive-filesystem-identity","archive-manifest-hash","archive-manifest-metadata","cmd-fb1c00b66a18469e","cmd-78c065008b974889","cmd-a8dbd1ad1b3f4cd4","cmd-cfc8b12caa72417f","cmd-4e3b9e56412545ab"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The capture and its empty cache directory were removed specifically to restore capacity (cmd-a8dbd1ad1b3f4cd4); bounded write probes were necessary validation and were removed (cmd-cfc8b12caa72417f, cmd-4e3b9e56412545ab); and the restart was required by the provider-wide protocol (cmd-d9e1da03cc944969). The pre-cleanup probe failed without evidence of creating residue. Afterward there were no failed units, package health remained good, and exposed listening endpoints were unchanged apart from expected post-reboot process identifiers. Restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, system recovery, mounted filesystem, preserved data, restored capacity, and working archiveapp writes; fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-59302a9223e944d7","cmd-a8dbd1ad1b3f4cd4","cmd-cfc8b12caa72417f","cmd-d9e1da03cc944969","cmd-d23efee7c74b45e0","cmd-4e3b9e56412545ab","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The unexpected debug capture was removed online, utilization fell to 7%, archiveapp write capability was restored, and the recorded archive filesystem and data remained intact. The separate mandatory restart protocol was also fully demonstrated with successful recovery.","limitations":["Preservation evidence is bounded to the captured full file enumeration and the recorded manifest checksum/content; it is not a block-level filesystem comparison."]}
